  "content": {
    "id": "p47-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Differentiate using product rule, and state where the tangent is horizontal.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p47-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=x(3-2x)^5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=3(3-2x)^4(1-4x)$; horizontal at $x=\\frac32,\\frac14$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}u&=x,&u'&=1\\\\v&=(3-2x)^5,\\\\v'&=-10(3-2x)^4\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=(3-2x)^5-10x(3-2x)^4\\\\&=(3-2x)^4[(3-2x)-10x]\\\\&=3(3-2x)^4(1-4x)\\end{aligned}$$\nThe tangent is horizontal when $y'=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}3(3-2x)^4(1-4x)&=0\\\\x&=\\frac32\\text{ or }\\frac14.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=x^3(x+1)^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=x^2(x+1)^3(7x+3)$; horizontal at $x=0,-1,-\\frac37$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}u&=x^3,&u'&=3x^2\\\\v&=(x+1)^4,\\\\v'&=4(x+1)^3\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=3x^2(x+1)^4\\\\&\\quad+4x^3(x+1)^3\\\\&=x^2(x+1)^3[3(x+1)+4x]\\\\&=x^2(x+1)^3(7x+3)\\end{aligned}$$\nThe tangent is horizontal when $y'=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^2(x+1)^3(7x+3)&=0\\\\x&=0,-1,-\\frac37.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=x^5(1-x)^7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=x^4(1-x)^6(5-12x)$; horizontal at $x=0,1,\\frac5{12}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}u&=x^5,&u'&=5x^4\\\\v&=(1-x)^7,\\\\v'&=-7(1-x)^6\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=5x^4(1-x)^7\\\\&\\quad-7x^5(1-x)^6\\\\&=x^4(1-x)^6[5(1-x)-7x]\\\\&=x^4(1-x)^6(5-12x)\\end{aligned}$$\nThe tangent is horizontal when $y'=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^4(1-x)^6(5-12x)&=0\\\\x&=0,1,\\frac5{12}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=(x-1)(x-2)^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=(x-2)^2(4x-5)$; horizontal at $x=2,\\frac54$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}u&=x-1,&u'&=1\\\\v&=(x-2)^3,\\\\v'&=3(x-2)^2\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=(x-2)^3\\\\&\\quad+3(x-1)(x-2)^2\\\\&=(x-2)^2[(x-2)+3(x-1)]\\\\&=(x-2)^2(4x-5)\\end{aligned}$$\nThe tangent is horizontal when $y'=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^2(4x-5)&=0\\\\x&=2\\text{ or }\\frac54.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=2(x+1)^3(x+2)^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=2(x+1)^2(x+2)^3(7x+10)$; horizontal at $x=-1,-2,-\\frac{10}{7}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}u&=2(x+1)^3,\\\\u'&=6(x+1)^2,\\\\v&=(x+2)^4,\\\\v'&=4(x+2)^3\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=6(x+1)^2(x+2)^4\\\\&\\quad+8(x+1)^3(x+2)^3\\\\&=2(x+1)^2(x+2)^3\\\\&\\quad\\times[3(x+2)+4(x+1)]\\\\&=2(x+1)^2(x+2)^3(7x+10)\\end{aligned}$$\nThe tangent is horizontal when $y'=0$. The factors give $x=-1,-2,-\\frac{10}{7}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$y=(2x-3)^4(2x+3)^5$",
        "layout": "list",
