        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=6(2x-3)^3(2x+3)^4(6x-1)$; horizontal at $x=\\frac32,-\\frac32,\\frac16$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}u&=(2x-3)^4,\\\\u'&=8(2x-3)^3,\\\\v&=(2x+3)^5,\\\\v'&=10(2x+3)^4\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=8(2x-3)^3(2x+3)^5\\\\&\\quad+10(2x-3)^4(2x+3)^4\\\\&=2(2x-3)^3(2x+3)^4\\\\&\\quad\\times[4(2x+3)+5(2x-3)]\\\\&=2(2x-3)^3(2x+3)^4(18x-3)\\\\&=6(2x-3)^3(2x+3)^4(6x-1)\\end{aligned}$$\nThe tangent is horizontal when $y'=0$. The factors give $x=\\frac32,-\\frac32,\\frac16$.",
